 "beats": [
  {
   "type": "title",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "globe",
   "text": "How did a four-hundred-year empire end in one summer?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Spain's empire began in 1492 and ended in 1898, in a war with the United States that lasted under four months."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "What was left of the empire by then?",
   "scene": "start",
   "date": "1895",
   "place": "Caribbean"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Cuba and Puerto Rico in the Caribbean, and the Philippines and Guam in the Pacific. And in 1895, Cuba rose up again."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Just across the water, Americans watched closely.",
   "scene": "cuba",
   "date": "1895",
   "place": "Cuba",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "What started the war?",
   "scene": "maine2",
   "date": "15 February 1898",
   "place": "Havana",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.45,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "The American battleship Maine blew up in Havana harbour. Two hundred and sixty-six men died."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "American newspapers blamed Spain. Remember the Maine! Later studies suggest it may have been a fire inside the ship."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "War came in April. At Manila, an American squadron wiped out Spain's Pacific fleet within hours.",
   "scene": "manila",
   "date": "1 May 1898",
   "place": "Manila",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "In July, Spain's Atlantic fleet tried to break out of Santiago de Cuba. Every ship was lost.",
   "scene": "santiago",
   "date": "3 July 1898",
   "place": "Santiago de Cuba",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "How did it end?",
   "scene": "paris",
   "date": "10 December 1898",
   "place": "Paris",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.45,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "By December it was over. Spain gave up Cuba, and handed Puerto Rico, Guam and the Philippines to the United States."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "So what did the map look like after?",
   "scene": "end",
   "date": "1899",
   "place": "The Americas"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "No Spanish flag left in the Americas. A year later, Spain sold its last Pacific islands to Germany."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "It had begun in 1492, with three small ships. Spaniards called its end, simply, the Disaster.",
   "scene": "landing",
   "date": "",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.2
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Next time: the republic that voted out a king. Like the video and follow History Sketches."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And tell us in the comments what you think!"
  },
  {
   "type": "end",
   "text": "Next: the republic that voted out a king",
   "sub": "Follow History Sketches"
  }
